  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description
    
    A palm-sized medallion of aurora-glass, heavier than its material accounts for, carved with interlocking pathways that correspond to no known map of the Berg. Under aurora-light or starlight it glows faint and steady; in ordinary darkness it dulls to the color of old bone. On documented occasions it has glowed without any external light source — three consecutive nights before the breach at the Fissured Smelt, and reportedly on each anniversary since. Visitors to the Dawn Terrace, the aurora-facing terrace complex where it was long enshrined, have reported unprompted luminescence during routine visits.
    
    When handled, nearby fire-braziers have been observed flickering in a three-two pattern — three short gutters, pause, two long flares. Those who carry the Medallion report a sympathetic pulse in their own flippers that they cannot suppress.
    
    ## Chain of Custody
    
    The Medallion's history is best understood as a sequence of holders, most of whom came to grief.
    
    | **Holder** | **Period** | **Outcome** |
    |---|---|---|
    | Iing zhixai'Ward, discoverer | Great Thaw | Excavated the Medallion at the Dawn Terrace, half-buried in deep ice. Believed it to be a tool. Her name has since been quietly effaced from the Dawn Terrace's public displays. |
    | The Wake-Singers, orca shaman cult | Faction Wars | Wore it in procession and sang to it as a relic. Circumstances of their acquisition are unrecorded. |
    | The Communion (elt-sworn), Nightshelf blood-cult | Pre-Clever Ice Age | The Communion's founders also sang to the Medallion. The Profun∴lapsum followed — whether caused by, coincident with, or channeled through those rites is disputed — and the Medallion went dark for three full seasons. |
    | Unnamed courier | Pre-theft | Carried the Medallion between civilizations before ☽'Iarlocias's theft. Never returned. His trade-name was retired without explanation — a Courier Corps practice reserved for confirmed deaths or irrecoverable disgrace. |
    | ☽'Iarlocias the Silent, Nightshelf mystic | Clever Ice Age | Stole it from the Communion's inner shrine and carried it into deep tunnels beyond sanctioned access. Returned frost-burned, speaking in an altered voice. Deliberately dulled the Medallion, wrapped it in Communion ceremonial thread, and abandoned it in her nest in the third cavern of ☽'secret Sanctninicaesis. Her stated reason: the Communion's blood-rites were waking something beneath the ice, or the Medallion was using the rites to wake itself, and the distinction had ceased to matter. |
    | ☽'Ilsancuia Depth-walker, Lector | Late career, final decade | Found the Medallion in ☽'Iarlocias's abandoned nest. Spent her remaining years restoring its luminescence — the records say she believed the artifact was *suffering*. Over time the glow ceased responding to ambient conditions and began responding to ☽'Ilsancuia directly. The pathways appeared to reveal memory-routes through buried architecture the Nightshelf had chosen to forget. She died while communing with it. |
    | ☽'Ilun the Refracted, ice-reader | Brief | Applied deprecated Aurora Stack ice-reading techniques to the Medallion's carvings and identified two distinct layers: a surface map tracing smuggling routes through the Nightshelf tunnels, and a deeper map — visible only under different light — showing approach vectors converging on deliberately dismantled defenses along the Stack's eastern ridge, including one route originating from the council tier. Murdered by operatives of Shadow-Broker Nyla, intelligence chief of the Midnight Claws, two nights after reporting these findings. |
    | Frost-ward Yunjoushong zhu'Eyrie, auditor | During Nyla investigation | Removed the Medallion from its Stillness-Bound enshrinement at the Dawn Terrace as evidence during her audit of Nyla's confession. Carried it toward Midway Shelf, bypassing internal authority she had reason to distrust. Last known position: the Midway Shelf approach. She has not reported since. |
    
    ## Current Status
    
    The Medallion's location is listed as **UNVERIFIED** in every subsequent intelligence assessment. Its deep-route mapping capability — potentially relevant to charting vectors through the Berg's unmapped interior — was flagged as a priority recovery asset. The Glow-Fissure Incursion Assessment produced by the Shadow-Walk Detachment ☽'Tertius noted the Medallion's loss as a material intelligence gap.
    
    No recovery operation has been mounted, or if one has, it has not been documented in any stratum I have access to.
    
    ## Observations on the Record
    
    The pattern is consistent enough to state plainly: every individual who held this artifact for an extended period either disappeared, died in connection with what it revealed, or returned fundamentally altered. Whether this constitutes a property of the artifact or a property of the knowledge it contains is a question the sources do not resolve. ☽'Iarlocias treated it as the former. ☽'Ilun's murder suggests the latter. ☽'Ilsancuia's case resists either explanation.
    
    The Dawn Terrace now displays the Medallion's history as heritage tourism. Iing zhixai'Ward's name does not appear on the signage.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771575555535_0", anchor: "half-buried in deep ice", text: "Deep ice at the Dawn Terrace dates to strata I would classify as pre-civilizational — well before any penguin settlement, let alone mapped infrastructure. Yet ☽'Ilun's later reading found Nightshelf smuggling routes and Aurora defense vectors carved into its pathways: architecture that post-dates the Clever Ice Age at earliest. Either Iing misidentified the stratum (she was a schismatic, not a glaciologist), or the ice compressed shallow deposits downward faster than expected at that site, or the pathways were not fixed at the time of carving. I have seen impressions in comparably deep strata that resist explanation. I note the displacement. I do not resolve it because I cannot.", type: :temporal, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575555535_1", anchor: "including one route originating from the council tier", text: "I noted in my Shadow-Broker Nyla entry that her predecessor was an Aurora penguin — not Nightshelf — and that the official histories were quietly amended. An approach vector through deliberately dismantled Aurora defenses, originating from the Aurora council tier, mapped onto an artifact that Nyla's operatives then killed to suppress. The Medallion did not create these routes. It recorded them. How extraordinary that someone carved their own treason into aurora-glass and trusted it to be mistaken for sacred geometry.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771575555535_2", anchor: "Circumstances of their acquisition are unrecorded", text: "A palm-sized penguin artifact in orca flippers during the Faction Wars. 'Unrecorded' is doing extraordinary work in that sentence.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575555535_3", anchor: "the distinction had ceased to matter", text: "The clearest thinking in this entire chain of custody, from the one holder the record dismisses as broken.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771575555535_4", anchor: "Last known position: the Midway Shelf approach. She has not reported since.", text: "The unnamed courier vanished carrying it between civilizations. Yunjoushong vanished carrying it toward Midway Shelf. Two holders, same trajectory, same silence. I find myself less interested in the artifact's properties than in what, exactly, is on that approach route that keeps swallowing people who carry inconvenient evidence.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
